Hi there,

I have a strange hardware problem based on a system with a UP1500
motherboard, which I picked up off of ebay earlier in the year.

Up until a couple of weeks ago the hardware was functioning fine, however I
had another P4 xeon system that I was fiddling with which I took the PSU
from the alpha and placed in this system due to the additional connectors on
this particular 400w psu. I placed a cheaper 300w psu in the alpha. Things
seemed to be functioning fine until I had the alpha on for some time when
the display went. At first I figured the Monitor had gone. Then after a
couple of days I recalled a review someone had written about this particular
cheap psu. SO I swapped the old 400w psu back. Things seemed to be working
fine again. However this has led on to another problem, now the UP1500 alpha
only seem to work when the pedestal tower case is on it's side, horizontal.
In a vertical position the machine starts up but there is no display.
However when it is horizontal it boots up fine, display et al.

I've tried everything I can think of to rectify this problem - reseating the
vga card, swapping vga cards,  reseating the memory, adjusting the internal
and external cables etc..

Does this possibly mean that the motherboard or the soldered cpu has some
kind of dry joint?

I think I recall someone else on this list having a simialar problem with an
XP1000.

Also if i start the machine on it's side and the let srm finish booting to
the prompt >> and then return the case to a vertical postion the prompt
ceases to work.

If anyone any ideas i be pleased to here them.

Also I have one other question - Does anyone know if there is any command in
the SRM to make the onboard sound on a UP1500 motherboard active?

I'm using Debian Sid on this particular machine and the boot up seems to
detect the SB compatible sound fine however under X I don't hear anything.
SB compatible sound is compiled in the stock woody 2.2 kernel.

Thanks for any help.

Kind regards,

Peter Watkinson
peter.watkinson1@ntlworld.com



