On Thu, Aug 14, 2003 at 11:39:56AM -0400, Jiann-Ming Su wrote:
> On Mon, 11 Aug 2003, Jean-Sébastien Guay wrote:
> 
> > Hello list,
> > 
> > I know I can't get official support from RedHat, Compaq or HP here, but
> > I thought I'd try this list to see if anyone had had these problems
> > before, and know the solutions. I must use MILO, because the system I'm
> > trying to install on is an Alpha XL-366, onto which I can't install the
> > SRM console and am stuck with AlphaBIOS.
> > 
> 
> My understanding is the RedHat 7.2 based distribution can only be installed
> with SRM.

Well, no.  I can serve as a counterexample as I personally installed
RH7.2 on some systems where only milo was available and helped other
people to do that.  It is true that this is not that straightforward, to
put it mildly, and that a default distribution kernel will not boot with
most milos as it is compiled with LEGACY_LOAD_ADDRESS off (there are
some milo variants which can cope with that and, if you are really
cannot replace your firmware with SRM, the best idea is to find
something like that for your platform if only possible).

My guess would be that kernel-milo-2.4.18-27.7.x.hp.alpha.rpm,
and possibly "HPWrapper", which can be found in updates to that distro,
may make that exercise easier but I did not have an opportunity to try.

  Michal



