You do may install RH 7.2 with milo. I've installed it on my 164SX
with milo just fairly.
Firts, get any milo that supports your system.
If you obtain 2.2.19 (latest) version you may boot just like

 boot hdc:/kernels/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 initrd=/images/cdrom.img

Or if you haven't latest version, you have to prepeare ramdisk
floppy (/images/ramdisk.img if I remember).
Then boot:

 boot hdc:/kernels/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

 After installation, you may put kernel from installation CD to a
 small FAT-16 partition or a diskette to make it available for milo.

Then boot your installed system like

 boot fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda1

 
 
 regards,
 Alexey



