I think you are a little sensitive here. If I substituted HP-UX for Microsoft would you feel better? This was just an example of a porting issue, it really was not an attack on MS. This would be an attack on MS.


| should we ignore "98-Percent Conformance to the ISO C++ Standard"

No, please do not ignore this. 98% is terrible. It is kind of like saying your water is 98% mercury-free. 

Compaq C++ is based on EDG 2.45 which supports all C++ features except export template. Most compiler writers think export template should be removed from the C++ standard. A proposal was recently submitted to remove it from the standard, however, it was rejected by the committee at the last standards meeting. Currently the only compiler to support export template is EDG 3.2. Our next compiler will be based on EDG 3.2, however, we will probably disable this feature. Give me a buzz when MS implements export templates and we will think about enabling it.

Now that was a diversion.

